-- A faulted block of 8 x 4 x 6 cells over the gas cap, oil zone and water
-- zone of a three-component oil saturated at its gas-oil contact, with
-- SWATINIT, per-cell endpoints (SWL, SWCR, SGL, SGU), rock compressibility
-- and the usual transmissibility edits: MULTREGT between the fault blocks,
-- EDITNNC on the fault's non-neighbour connections, and MULTIPLY on TRANX,
-- TRANY and TRANZ in the EDIT section.  The eastern block has the higher SWL
-- and SGL 0.03.
--
-- Above the water-oil contact SWATINIT lies halfway between SWL and SWCR,
-- except in column (2,2), where it lies below SWL, and in the last ten
-- metres above the contact, where it rises to 0.70 and the water is mobile.
-- Water is injected low in the western block and produced with the oil in
-- the eastern one, so it reaches the producer only across the fault.  The
-- compositional flow equations do not include capillary pressure yet, so
-- the mobile water above the contact is not held in place.
-- FAULT_TRANMULT_ENDSCALE is the same block without capillary pressure.

